  "report": "Implementation review passed; operator acceptance remains separate.\n\nACCEPTED. OBSERVED: F-CS-002 is closed. support.rs now re-exports both is_vendored_path and VENDORED_SEGMENTS from the sole classification definition. The #[allow(unused_imports)] is justified locally: support is pub(crate), therefore the re-export is not externally visible and VENDORED_SEGMENTS has no in-crate consumer. It preserves the allocated forwarding surface while keeping the deny-warnings gate meaningful; no fake consumer, visibility change, dependency edge, or additional abstraction was introduced.\n\nOBSERVED architecture: generated_sniff records a deterministic Layer-0 file fact at the content-aware index point and refresh carries that stored fact forward. Storage deliberately retains the full certificate row set and merely carries file facts. Pure agent logic applies one post-read predicate before sort/truncation, derives the scoped count from retained rows, and emits a typed ComplexityScope. This serves the VISION: the default orientation shows the repository's own code while explicitly stating what was excluded and how --include-all reveals it, rather than implying completeness.\n\nOBSERVED abstractions are earned. ComplexityScope has two mutually exclusive states, Production{excluded_count} and All; current users are the complexity aggregator and two DTO fixtures; axis: fixed scope variants with growing readers; rejected alternative: boolean plus conditionally-valid excluded_count. classification::vendored_path is the single predicate/segment-list home for the agent aggregator and daemon quality/docs/orient consumers; axis: shared classification rule across those current consumers; rejected alternative: duplicate predicates that could drift. No new crate edge or cycle was introduced.\n\nOBSERVED checkout witnesses: codegraph parser.c:1 is /* Automatically @generated by tree-sitter */; poco bison_parser.cpp:1 is /* A Bison parser, made by GNU Bison 3.8.2.  */; codegraph worker-configuration.d.ts:1 is // Generated by wrangler. DO NOT EDIT.; and leveldb table/block.cc:5 is // Decodes the blocks generated by block_builder.cc. The first three are within the frozen first-eight-line marker rule; the leveldb line explains why generated by is excluded. OBSERVED residual witness: codegraph __tests__/generated-flag-index.test.ts:5 quotes a DO NOT EDIT banner. BUILDER-EXECUTED corpus captures report these generated/test/vendored rows are excluded by default and visible under --include-all, including repo-graph dispatch_op and compose_dependency_summaries; the latter remains an honestly reported pre-existing deps-segment residual. BUILDER-EXECUTED captures also report the intended codegraph, poco, repo-graph, and leveldb before/after headlines and store-predicate seams.\n\nOBSERVED scope: git status lists exactly the 27 allocated Rust paths; git diff --check HEAD is clean. BUILDER-EXECUTED evidence reports all CS-C01..C16 passed. The workspace-wide suite, smoke protocol, and isolated dogfood remain the operator gate specified by CLAUDE.md, not a missing builder requirement.\n\nManager interpretation by in-place-manager: The reviewer's message is a complete implementation review whose only off-shape part is the subject block (the runtime reported subject-mismatch: the reviewer echoed candidate/verification identities that do not match the derived ones for this cycle). Interpretation drops the subject and reshapes nothing: result, the 20 obligation, 16 check and 27 path assessments, findings, decisions and report are the reviewer's own text. Source provider run review-COMPLEXITY-SCOPE-1-1; retained output .agent-manager/slices/COMPLEXITY-SCOPE-1/review-1.json sha256:24a8b7bf108d058829552c700852eb73b1eace5341d121404b187b9a4a6a26bf. The provider remains the performer; this interpretation is not independent execution evidence."
